<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bacharach</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bacharach is a small town on the left bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland-palatinate">Rhineland-Palatinate</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it belonged to the counts palatine of the Rhine, who levied tolls on river traffic there, and it was a leading market for Rhine wine. Its half-timbered houses, town walls and Stahleck Castle make it part of the Upper Middle Rhine Valley World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bacharach.jpg" alt="Bacharach" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jiuguang Wang · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bacharach_from_the_Postenturm.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
